{
  "dom_id": "question-216577",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Select the correct options in the truth table below and use this to determine whether $¬(X⇔Y)⇒[(X∧¬Y)∨(¬X∧Y)]$ is a tautology.\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X⇔Y)\\,$ | $\\,(X∧¬Y)∨(¬X∧Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X↔Y)⇒[(X∧¬Y)∨(¬X∧Y)]\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nAccording to the table, $¬(X⇔Y)⇒[(X∧¬Y)∨(¬X∧Y)]$ \n{{field-5}}\nalways true. Therefore, it \n{{field-6}} \na tautology.",
